# The slot back-pointer of issue #266, as a patch against include/ankerl/unordered_dense.h.
#
# It lives here and not in the header because it lost: see notes/index-design.md, "A slot
# back-pointer, re-tested across the cache boundary". The header keeps one configuration, the way
# scripts/ab/window.cpp keeps the sliding window out of it -- and this stays so the numbers can be
# re-taken rather than believed.
#
# What it does: one packed slot number per value, parallel to m_values, so that finish_erase can
# repoint the moved element's slot directly instead of hashing its key a second time and walking to
# it. Ten maintenance sites: place_group, move_home, the rehash, place_element_at, emplace,
# increase_size's two failure paths, replace and its pipelined half, extract, and the copy, move and
# swap. Guarded by ANKERL_UNORDERED_DENSE_SLOT_BACK_POINTER, which defaults to 0, so applying the
# patch alone changes nothing; scripts/ab/back_pointer.sh defines it for its own copy of the header.
#
# It applies to include/ankerl/unordered_dense.h as of commit 7c5779f2e331. When it stops applying,
# `git show 7c5779f2e331:include/ankerl/unordered_dense.h` is the header it was measured against,
# so the numbers stay re-takeable rather than merely dated.
#
#   git apply scripts/ab/back_pointer.patch      # to run the unit tests against it:
#   CXXFLAGS=-DANKERL_UNORDERED_DENSE_SLOT_BACK_POINTER=1 meson setup builddir/bp && ninja -C builddir/bp
#
# 831 of 835 test cases pass that way, under clang, gcc and ASan+UBSan. The four that do not are
# `mutated_key_found_by_the_backfill_terminates`, which requires the backfill to diagnose a key the
# caller mutated through an iterator -- a walk that cannot go wrong when there is no walk.
